 "existingHosts": "No Core, Runtime, Package.swift or Swift change",
 "review": "Round 1 (independent, read-only): medium: a lane waiting at the gate could take an undefined file at the list's end and reject (the status left on screen); medium: the gate could turn the download serial when the program reads ahead (a player starting a match before the prefetch ends); low: failures counted as loaded, no cleanup at the end, the order after the startup package (alphabetical: OriginalCatalog first, which is also the first package the loading cycle reads), naming, docstring, one run each. Fixed (the gate holds all lanes only until the first frame), 3 runs each. Round 2: OK.",
 "boundaries": [
  "Bandwidth-bound lower bounds: the test server adds no round-trip delay; a loading cycle starting before the prefetch ends over a real link is unmeasured",
  "4 lanes tuned for HTTP/1.x (6 connections per host); conservative on HTTP/2",
  "Files the program already cached are read again from the cache by the lanes (no download), passing through the page's main thread — a possible frame-time cost on slow devices, unmeasured",
  "A static config without the canvas does not prefetch (web_app.py always sets the canvas)",
  "WebKit gets no prefetch (its synchronous reads miss the cache)"
 ]
}